            <div xml:id="d504">

                <pb facs="0838" n="718" xml:id="pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Czechoslovakia/198</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Czechoslovak Minister (Veverka) to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-12-15">December 15,
                        1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: In reply to Your Excellency’s note
                    of December 13th, 1932, and following the suggestion contained therein, I have
                    the honor to state that the Czechoslovak Government, in view of circumstances
                    presented in this note, has decided to pay the December installment.</p>
                <p>In bringing this decision to your attention, I am instructed to recall and stress
                    again all the considerations, conclusions and serious consequences mentioned in
                    my previous notes.</p>
                <p>I also take the liberty to point out that this payment constitutes in the utmost
                    self-denial of the Czechoslovak people their final effort to meet the obligation
                    under such extremely unfavorable circumstances.</p>
                <p>It is, therefore, the profound conviction of the Czechoslovak Government that
                    only negotiations entered into at the earliest possible date concerning the
                    reconsideration and revision, and also the inclusion of this last installment
                    into the forthcoming arrangement can bring some alleviation to the present most
                    distressing situation.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ferdinand Veverka</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
